# Export rules for the public snapshot sync (.gitea/workflows/public-sync.yml).
#
# .gitignore has NO effect on files that are already tracked. These
# export-ignore rules are what actually keep internal files out of the curated
# public snapshot, so anything built with `git archive` cannot leak them by
# accident. The workflow asserts the result rather than trusting it.
#
# Kept out of the public repo:
#   .gitea/            this instance's CI; meaningless off-site
#   .github/           upstream's GitHub-Actions CI, unmodified and unused here.
#                      Publishing it would ship a workflow pointing at a
#                      reusable workflow this fork does not own.
#   HANDOFF.md         operational notes: internal hostname, LAN IP, KB UUID,
#                      CA path. Session history, not documentation.
#   README.local.md    same, in table form: instance URLs, CA path, KB id.
#   plan.md/PLAN.md    working documents. They describe the repo as it was when
#                      written and then contradict the code. The durable record
#                      is the PR that implemented the work.
#   scripts/           publish tooling only, and it no longer exists: the publish
#                      step is .gitea/workflows/public-sync.yml. Kept as an
#                      export-ignore rule so a future script dropped in here
#                      cannot reach the snapshot by default.
scripts/               export-ignore
.gitea/                export-ignore
.github/               export-ignore
HANDOFF.md             export-ignore
README.local.md        export-ignore
plan.md                export-ignore
PLAN.md                export-ignore
